          "text": "CH'ÊN Shih-kuan 陳世倌 (T. 秉之, H. 蓮宇) Nov. 15, 1680-1758, May 21, official, was a native of Hai-ning, Chekiang. He received his chin-shih degree in 1703 and became a compiler in the Hanlin Academy (1706).",
